==English==
{{was wotd|2010|October|16}}
[[File:Chambers 1908 Toggle.png|thumb|A '''toggle''' (sense 1)]]
[[File:Knebelverschluss IMG 5104.JPG|thumb|A '''toggle''' (sense 2)]]

===Etymology===
Of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. Possible alteration of {{suffix|en|tug|gloss1=to pull|le}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɒɡ.əl/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɑ.ɡəl/|a=GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-toggle.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɔɡ.əl/|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-toggle.ogg|a=Queensland}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɒɡ.əl/|a=NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɡəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} A wooden or metal pin, short rod, crosspiece or similar, fixed transversely in the eye of a rope or chain to be secured to any other loop, ring, or [[bight]], e.g. a [[sea painter]] to a [[lifeboat]].
# {{lb|en|in particular|fashion}} A [[rod]]-shaped [[button]] [[bound]] with [[slack]] to the [[fabric]].
# A [[toggle switch]].
# An appliance for transmitting force at right angles to its direction.
# A horizontal piece of wood that is placed on a door, flat, or other wooden structure, but is not on one of the edges of the structure.
# A fastener that has flaps that align vertically to penetrate a surface and then spread out to secure the fastener in position, e.g. a [[molly bolt]].
# {{lb|en|skydiving}} A loop of webbing or a dowel affixed to the end of the steering/brake lines of a parachute providing the pilot with a means of control.

